# Compile-only smoke test corpus: tests/cmm-pass/<name>.c-- sources that are
# expected to compile successfully with the default (x86) backend.
#
# tests/cmm-pass/ and tests/cmm-fail/ are themselves the classification
# (the directory a file lives in says what it's supposed to do) - this
# manifest is a belt-and-suspenders cross-check, not the source of truth.
# run-compile.sh errors out if this list and `ls cmm-pass/*.c--` ever
# disagree, so a file dropped into the wrong directory (or a name left here
# after being moved to cmm-fail/) can't go unnoticed.
#
# A name here can still legitimately FAIL today: that just means it is a
# known, not-yet-fixed gap (see cmm-pass/output/<name>.s2_but_should_work)
# rather than an intentional negative test - those live in cmm-fail/ and
# cmm-fail.tests instead.
#
# One name per line, no extension, no directory (always tests/cmm-pass/<name>.c--).

